{"id":"n1-039","title":"Noun + というもの (~ to iu mono)","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Used to express a generic concept: 'all ~', 'any ~ of that kind'.","longExplanation":"The grammar pattern 'Noun + というもの' refers to the entirety or general nature of that noun—often implying 'all of this category' or 'this thing called...'. It can also highlight a universal truth about the noun mentioned.","formation":"Noun + というもの","examples":[{"jp":"子供というものは、毎日たくさん遊びます。","romaji":"Kodomo to iu mono wa, mainichi takusan asobimasu.","en":"Children, as a group, play a lot every day.","words":[{"surface":"子供","vocabId":"1307850","reading":"こども"},{"surface":"という","vocabId":null},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"毎日","vocabId":"1524720","reading":"まいにち"},{"surface":"たくさん","vocabId":"1415870","reading":"たくさん"},{"surface":"遊び","vocabId":"1542070","reading":"あそび","baseForm":"遊ぶ"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1,2]},{"jp":"大学生というものは研究に時間をたくさんかけます。","romaji":"Daigakusei to iu mono wa kenkyuu ni jikan o takusan kakemasu.","en":"University students spend a lot of time on research.","words":[{"surface":"大学生","vocabId":"1413260","reading":"だいがくせい"},{"surface":"という","vocabId":null},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"研究","vocabId":"1258520","reading":"けんきゅう"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"時間","vocabId":"1315920","reading":"じかん"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"たくさん","vocabId":"1415870","reading":"たくさん"},{"surface":"かけ","vocabId":"1590040","reading":"かけ","baseForm":"かける"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1,2]},{"jp":"日本文化というものは伝統的なものと新しいものが混ざっています。","romaji":"Nihon bunka to iu mono wa dentouteki na mono to atarashii mono ga mazatte imasu.","en":"Japanese culture is a mixture of traditional and new.","words":[{"surface":"日本","vocabId":"1582710","reading":"にほん"},{"surface":"文化","vocabId":"1505120","reading":"ぶんか"},{"surface":"という","vocabId":null},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"伝統","vocabId":"1442260","reading":"でんとう"},{"surface":"的","vocabId":"1437260","reading":"てき"},{"surface":"な","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"新しい","vocabId":"1361490","reading":"あたらしい"},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"混ざっ","vocabId":"1603920","reading":"まざる","baseForm":"混ざる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2,3]},{"jp":"別れというものはいつも悲しいものです。","romaji":"Wakare to iu mono wa itsumo kanashii mono desu.","en":"Goodbyes are always sad.","words":[{"surface":"別れ","vocabId":"1509490","reading":"わかれ"},{"surface":"という","vocabId":null},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いつも","vocabId":"1188890","reading":"いつも"},{"surface":"悲しい","vocabId":"1483190","reading":"かなしい"},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1,2]}]}